// Space data for the Space Race app.
//
// Each row: [name, group, year, country, description, clue 3, clue 4, clue 5, wikipedia page]
//   year:    the big year (launch, first flight, birth year for people), or "" for planets, stars and galaxies
//   country: a key from SPACE_COUNTRIES, or "" for things in nature
//   Clues 1 and 2 are built automatically from the year, country and group (see buildClues in index.html),
//   so the "Who Am I?" game always has 5 clues that go from easy-to-guess-wrong to a big giveaway.
//   wikipedia page: where tools/fetch_images.py looks for a free photo (the credit goes in credits.js).
//
// Images: space-images/<name in lower case, spaces and marks turned into underscores>.webp, 800 x 600.
// Until a picture exists the app draws a coloured placeholder.
//
// Facts about the future were checked on 11 October 2026. Space plans change often, so check them again before updating.

